 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Inventing is not discovering",
     "texto": [
      "**Ciencia** moves forward with research: a **científico** does an **experimento** in the **laboratorio** and gets a **resultado**.\n\n- **Inventar** is to create something new: an **invento**.\n- **Descubrir** is to find something that already existed: a **descubrimiento**.\n- **Demostrar** is to prove that something is true.\n\nSometimes a great **avance** comes **por casualidad**. To tell the story of a discovery we use the past and the passive: **fue descubierta**, **se descubrió**, **se han salvado**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "The passive: fue descubierta, se descubrió",
     "texto": [
      "To tell what was discovered and not who did it, use the passive:\n\n- **ser** + participle: **la penicilina fue descubierta en 1928**. The participle agrees with the subject (descubierta, descubierto, descubiertos).\n- **se** + verb: **se descubrió la penicilina**; **se han salvado millones de vidas**. It is the most common form in speech.\n\nThe participle of **descubrir** is irregular: **descubierto**."
     ],
